    <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the coefficients a, b and c of the interface derivative reconstruction method for a given <ref refid="structInterface" kindref="compound">Interface</ref> between two patches. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class specialises <ref refid="classDerivReconstructionCoeffs" kindref="compound">DerivReconstructionCoeffs</ref> using the information stored in the <ref refid="structInterface" kindref="compound">Interface</ref> (perpendicular grids, B-splines and extremities of the two Edges). It also provides patch-based accessors and handles the change of sign of the cross-derivatives when the orientations of the two patches do not agree.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InterfaceType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The interface between two patches where we want to compute the derivatives. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
